<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">In
February of 2017, the Company purchased property, including vineyard land, bare land and structures in the Dundee Hills AVA under terms
that included a 15 year note payable with quarterly payments of $42,534 at 6%. The note may be called by the owner, up to the outstanding
balance, with 180 days written notice. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, the Company had a balance of $<span id="xdx_907_eus-gaap--NotesPayableCurrent_iI_c20251231_zqIIxv4dFbk3"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:NotesPayableCurrent" contextRef="AsOf2025-12-31" id="Fact000565" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="0" unitRef="USD">884,221</ix:nonFraction></span> and $<span id="xdx_904_eus-gaap--NotesPayableCurrent_iI_c20241231_z1ORsRRTCNmh"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:NotesPayableCurrent" contextRef="AsOf2024-12-31" id="Fact000566" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="0" unitRef="USD">995,968</ix:nonFraction></span>, respectively,
due on this note.</span></p>

